      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right—poetry doesn't fix anything. And I'm not going to pretend it does. But \"stopping\" doesn't have to mean giving up on yourself; it can mean putting the fight down for a while and just sitting in the rubble without forcing yourself to rebuild.  \n\nThe mountain always wins, sure—but you're not the mountain. You're the one who keeps walking, even when the path is gone. That's not weakness; that's a stubbornness you haven't given yourself credit for.",
